{"ld": 1287, "paper": "SP516", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Support Workforce Development by Establishing the Housing Stability Fund", "sponsor_id": "s-larsen-daughtry-matthea", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-abdi-mana", "s-bennett-richard", "h-dhalac-deqa", "s-duson-jill", "h-gattine-andrew", "h-rana-ambureen", "s-rotundo-margaret", "s-talbot-ross-rachel", "h-yusuf-yusuf"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This bill establishes the Housing Stability Support Program and the Housing Stability Fund within the Maine State Housing Authority. The Maine State Housing Authority is 2106 required to delegate administration of the program to one or more of the following: a 2117 designated community action agency as described by the Maine Revised Statutes, Title 22, 2128 section 5324; a municipal housing authority; or any other qualified entity as determined by 2139 the Maine State Housing Authority. The program provides rental assistance, paid directly to a landlord, for tenants with household incomes of less than 30% of the median income for the area at the time of application for assistance, except when the assistance payment is for a security deposit required for a new lease or rental agreement. Rental assistance paid through the program may not exceed $300 per month. The maximum amount of total assistance per household is $3,000. The bill provides for an ongoing appropriation of $1,900,000 annually to support the purposes of the program.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0516&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2025-07-07", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-07-07"}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN128701.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (L